    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nHow does one disable `indentscope` on `InsertEnter`? I need this for `Zen Mode`. \r\n\r\nIn particular, the disable function in the code below doesn't work. \r\n\r\nAlso looked at the docs and didn't find any `enable` or `disable` APIs. \r\n\r\nAny pointers are appreciated.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal function disable_mini_indentscope()\r\n  vim.b.miniidentscope_disable = true\r\n  local status, indent = pcall(require, \"mini.indentscope\")\r\n  if status then\r\n    indent.undraw()\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal function enable_mini_indentscope()\r\n  vim.b.miniidentscope_disable = false\r\n  local status, indent = pcall(require, \"mini.indentscope\")\r\n  if status then\r\n    indent.auto_draw()\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n```",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hello,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">How does one disable <code class=\"notranslate\">indentscope</code> on <code class=\"notranslate\">InsertEnter</code>? I need this for <code class=\"notranslate\">Zen Mode</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">In particular, the disable function in the code below doesn't work.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also looked at the docs and didn't find any <code class=\"notranslate\">enable</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">disable</code> APIs.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Any pointers are appreciated.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"local function disable_mini_indentscope()\n  vim.b.miniidentscope_disable = true\n  local status, indent = pcall(require, &quot;mini.indentscope&quot;)\n  if status then\n    indent.undraw()\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function enable_mini_indentscope()\n  vim.b.miniidentscope_disable = false\n  local status, indent = pcall(require, &quot;mini.indentscope&quot;)\n  if status then\n    indent.auto_draw()\n  end\nend\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">disable_mini_indentscope</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">miniidentscope_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">true</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">status</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">indent</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">pcall</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.indentscope<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">status</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">indent</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">undraw</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span> <span class=\"pl-en\">enable_mini_indentscope</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">b</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">miniidentscope_disable</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">local</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">status</span>, <span class=\"pl-smi\">indent</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">pcall</span>(<span class=\"pl-c1\">require</span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>mini.indentscope<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>)\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">status</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-smi\">indent</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">auto_draw</span>()\n  <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n<span class=\"pl-k\">end</span></pre></div>",
    "bodyText": "Hello,\nHow does one disable indentscope on InsertEnter? I need this for Zen Mode.\nIn particular, the disable function in the code below doesn't work.\nAlso looked at the docs and didn't find any enable or disable APIs.\nAny pointers are appreciated.\nlocal function disable_mini_indentscope()\n  vim.b.miniidentscope_disable = true\n  local status, indent = pcall(require, \"mini.indentscope\")\n  if status then\n    indent.undraw()\n  end\nend\n\nlocal function enable_mini_indentscope()\n  vim.b.miniidentscope_disable = false\n  local status, indent = pcall(require, \"mini.indentscope\")\n  if status then\n    indent.auto_draw()\n  end\nend",
